  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =256 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}(256)=64 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1}{4}(64)=16 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}(16)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{4}=4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
